PY  - 2021
LA  - eng
DO  - 10.1097/WNO.0000000000000920
AN  - 32141979
UR  - https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32141979/
AB  - A 36-year-old apparently healthy man presented with acute onset of diplopia.  Examination demonstrated left sixth nerve palsy with 3 retinal hemorrhages noted in one eye. Gadolinium-enhanced high-resolution skull base MRI revealed left sixth nerve enhancement involving the cisternal segment. Complete blood count, cerebrospinal fluid analysis, bone marrow biopsy, and flow cytometry confirmed acute T-cell lymphoblastic leukemia with central nervous system involvement. This case demonstrates the value of high-resolution MRI in the evaluation of cranial nerve palsy in young adults and also emphasizes the importance of systemic work up in these cases, particularly when retinal findings are present.
