AB  - The myelodysplastic syndromes (MDS) are a diverse group of clonal hematopoietic  stem cell disorders characterized by cytopenias. Patients have a risk of developing acute leukemia though most succumb to complications of low blood counts. Over the past decade many novel treatments have been developed and investigation of new agents is ongoing. In this article, we discuss the classification and prognostic systems that are used in MDS, the agents available for treatment of MDS as well as review supportive and palliative care options for patients who are not candidates for, or opt against, newer treatment strategies.
