AB  - Tissue polypeptide antigen (TPA) in serum was measured at diagnosis in 27  patients with acute nonlymphocytic leukemia (ANLL) (1 FAB M0, 1 M1, 10 M2, 7 M3, 5 M4, 1 M5, 1 M6 and 1 MU). Statistical analysis disclosed a close correlation of TPA level with age (P < 0.01), hemoglobin level (P < 0.05), therapeutic response (P < 0.01) and the length of survival after the initial diagnosis (P < 0.02). A significant difference in TPA level was present between patients with complete remission and those with poor response. To our knowledge, this is the first report to prove a correlation of TPA level with therapeutic response and the length of survival in ANLL.
