AB  - An autopsy case of acute megakaryocytic leukemia (AMKL) is presented. The bone  marrow was hypercellular with proliferation of three lineages, especially megakaryocytes. Immunohistochemical examination revealed many platelet glycoprotein IIb/IIIa (GP IIb/IIIa)-positive blast cells in bone marrow. The proportion of the blasts was 26.4% by tissue hemogram. GP IIb/IIIa-positive blasts and megakaryoblasts were deposited massively in lymph nodes. Immunohistochemistry against GP IIb/IIIa and tissue hemograms by paraffin section are needed to diagnose AMKL by postmortem examination, since the identification of ultrastructural platelet peroxidase in autopsy materials is difficult.
